description:
Edit repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts to use the trace response that is currently captured and discarded.

The file already contains, at the compose trace emission, a variable assigned from the awaited fetch whose URL path is v2/activities/executions. That variable is never read anywhere in the file, so the emission blocks on the trace store and gains nothing. This single edit makes it useful by logging the execution identifier the trace store returned, which is the address by which that row can later be graded.

Replace this exact line:
    }).catch(() => { /* trace-store unreachable — never fail the compose */ });

with exactly these lines:
    }).catch(() => null);
    if (traceRes && traceRes.ok) {
      const traceBody = (await traceRes.json().catch(() => null)) as { data?: { execution_id?: string } } | null;
      const emittedId = traceBody?.data?.execution_id;
      if (typeof emittedId === "string" && emittedId.length > 0) {
        console.log(`[feature-compose] trace emission persisted execution_id=${emittedId}`);
      }
    }

That line occurs exactly once in the file. The existing behaviour is preserved: on any trace-store failure the catch yields null and the block is skipped, the enclosing catch is untouched, and the 5000ms AbortSignal timeout is unchanged, so a trace-store problem still cannot fail a compose.

This is a single replacement. Make no other change and touch no other file.

